    "leftUpperLeg",
    "rightUpperLeg",
    "weapon"
  ],
  "usage": "Use for a sword slash, melee attack, or tebasan pedang on the current Rhino rig. Duration is 48 frames at 30 FPS (1.6 seconds). All keyframes use linear interpolation for crisp action timing. This is a one-shot action, not a loop; the starting and ending poses differ. The sword is attached to the right hand (bone ID 3), so wrist rotation directly controls the blade. The source rig has two bones named right_arm: ID 2 is the upper arm (parent ID 1), and ID 3 is the right hand (parent ID 2, carrying sword ID 9). Apply tracks by boneId on this rig; name-only mapping cannot distinguish these tracks. Eyes and sword retain their local transforms and inherit their parents' motion.",
